# /etc/omniswarm/providers.env  (root:root 0600)
# Operator provider keys for the worker units. Intentionally empty.
#
# OmniSwarm charges users nothing and pays for no user's review. A hosted
# review runs only on the signed-in account's own NEAR AI Cloud key (preset
# account-nearai), sealed in Postgres under ACCOUNT_KEYS_SECRET (worker.env).
# Z.AI and OpenRouter are removed (docs/spec/DECISIONS.md OD-26).
#
# `./bin/audit local --provider nearai` reads NEARAI_API_KEY from the
# operator's own shell, not from this file.
#
# The file stays because the worker unit loads it (EnvironmentFile=) and
# secrets.sh installs it. Read by systemd for the worker units only. The API
# container, nginx, Postgres and the sandbox never see it (`npm run
# check:infra` fails if a compose service declares a provider key). Keep it
# empty: a key here (NEARAI_API_KEY included) would reach the engine for a job on
# the `hosted` preset, and the operator would pay for it. secrets-check.mjs
# refuses any variable in this file.
